            "notes": "Checks for unexpectedly read-only mounted filesystems, such as a root filesystem that switched to read-only due to disk errors. Ignores ramfs, squashfs (snapd), and other pseudo-filesystems by default. Additional mount points can be excluded via --extend-ignore, additional filesystem types via --extend-ignore-fstype. Alerts when a read-only filesystem is detected that should be writable.",
